---
import LegalPage from "../components/identity/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  { id: "scope", label: "Who and what this covers" },
  { id: "processing", label: "Information and purposes" },
  { id: "providers", label: "Recipients and transfers" },
  { id: "retention", label: "Retention" },
  { id: "rights", label: "Your rights" },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="How Abstract Machines handles company-website visits and enquiries."
  sections={sections}
  meta={[{ label: "Updated", value: "3 November 2026" }]}
  contactEmail="privacy@absmach.eu"
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    <p>
      This notice covers the company website and enquiries sent to Abstract
      Machines.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
  <section id="scope">
    <h2>Who and what this covers</h2>
    <p>
      Abstract Machines SAS, 141 Quai de Valmy, 75010 Paris, France, is the
      controller for these activities. Contact: <a
        href="mailto:privacy@absmach.eu">privacy@absmach.eu</a
      >. Product processing is described in the relevant service notice,
      including <a href="https://atomicapp.dev/legal/privacy/"
        >Atomic’s privacy notice</a
      >. Processing on a customer’s behalf is governed by the applicable data
      processing agreement.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="processing">
    <h2>Information and purposes</h2>
    <p>
      Our contact form collects your name, email, message and enquiry topic,
      plus any organisation or product information you choose to provide.
      Required fields let us respond; without them the form cannot be submitted.
      Hosting and abuse protection process IP addresses, browser signals and
      request metadata.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Enquiries: steps you request before a contract, or our legitimate
        interest in answering business and other correspondence.
      </li>
      <li>
        Website delivery, security and abuse prevention: our legitimate interest
        in operating and protecting the website.
      </li>
      <li>
        Legal records and claims: applicable legal obligations or our legitimate
        interest in establishing and defending legal rights.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Sending an enquiry does not subscribe you to marketing. Avoid sending
      unnecessary sensitive information or third-party personal data.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="providers">
    <h2>Recipients and transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Authorized staff, website hosting/security providers and email providers
      receive information necessary for their tasks. Cloudflare hosts the site
      and provides Turnstile abuse protection on the contact form. See <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
        >Cloudflare’s privacy information</a
      > for its processing. Advisers and authorities may receive information where
      necessary for legal matters.
    </p>
    <p>
      Providers may process information outside the European Economic Area,
      including in the United States. Such transfers require an applicable
      adequacy decision or appropriate safeguards, such as EU standard
      contractual clauses with necessary supplementary measures. Contact our
      privacy address for the safeguards applicable to your data and a copy.
    </p>
    <p>
      Hosting and abuse protection may use browser storage necessary for their
      operation. Links to external services, including YouTube videos, open
      those services under their own privacy information.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="retention">
    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Correspondence is kept while needed to handle the enquiry and related
      follow-up. Security information is kept while needed to detect,
      investigate and address incidents. Records needed for a contract, legal
      obligation or claim are retained for the applicable purpose and statutory
      period, with access restricted as appropriate.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="rights">
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Where applicable, you may request access, correction, deletion,
      restriction or portability, object to processing based on legitimate
      interests or to direct marketing, withdraw consent without affecting prior
      lawful processing, and give instructions concerning your data after death.
    </p>
    <p>
      Write to <a href="mailto:privacy@absmach.eu">privacy@absmach.eu</a>.
      Requests are handled within the GDPR deadlines; any permitted extension
      will be explained within the initial deadline. You may complain directly
      to the <a href="https://www.cnil.fr/fr/plaintes">CNIL</a> or another competent
      supervisory authority.
    </p>
    <p>
      This notice may be updated as practices change. Further information or
      consent will be provided or sought where required by law.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
